WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(studio audience cheering)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- All right.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.999
- Hello, hello.

00:00:04.986 --> 00:00:05.857
- They love you.

00:00:05.857 --> 00:00:06.960
They love you.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.793
Oh my God.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.230
Well, welcome back to the show.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.610
This time we came to you.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.443
- Thank you.

00:00:12.443 --> 00:00:13.276
- Yeah.

00:00:13.276 --> 00:00:14.109
- So much for coming to New York.

00:00:14.109 --> 00:00:14.942
- You didn't have to travel far.

00:00:14.942 --> 00:00:15.775
- No, it's the A train.

00:00:15.775 --> 00:00:16.608
I took the A train to 59th Street.

00:00:16.608 --> 00:00:17.441
- I know.

00:00:17.441 --> 00:00:18.274
- It was great.

00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:19.107
- That's why- I've been
here for like a month.

00:00:19.107 --> 00:00:19.940
I love the subway.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:20.773
My kids love it too.

00:00:20.773 --> 00:00:22.830
They think it's so cool that
they hate getting in cars now.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.470
And I'm like, sometimes
it's nice to get in a car,

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.850
but like they love the subway.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.500
So wait, I heard that
you took your son's class

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.333
on a field trip.

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:30.750
I'm about to do a field
trip with my daughter.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.583
- I did.

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:33.617
My, my son's class was
obsessed with Greek myths,

00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:35.940
and this whole second grade class.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.620
Greek myths and Greek heroes.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.750
And so I took them to go
see "Hadestown" on Broadway.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.620
Yeah, there we are.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.453
(studio audience cheering)

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:43.300
- [Kelly] Yeah, that's so cool.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.133
- And it was, it was me,

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:47.548
and 26 second graders and their parents.

00:00:47.548 --> 00:00:48.660
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.493
- Which was fun.

00:00:49.493 --> 00:00:51.120
We really, it was it was a loud matinee,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.830
for the cast of "Hadestown."

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.060
- So was your family involved

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.410
with your school projects
when you were a kid?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.243
- Yes

00:00:56.243 --> 00:00:58.473
- [Kelly] Do you, do you
get involved with your kids?

00:00:58.473 --> 00:00:59.306
- Yes, I did.

00:00:59.306 --> 00:01:02.460
We, my son and I actually made a video

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.008
for my wife's 40th birthday.

00:01:04.008 --> 00:01:04.841
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:04.841 --> 00:01:05.880
- And he wrote the whole thing

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.758
and I edited it with my
friend, Alex Horowitz.

00:01:07.758 --> 00:01:08.591
But yeah.

00:01:08.591 --> 00:01:09.591
- Yeah.

00:01:09.591 --> 00:01:11.340
- But my parents totally, like I did a,

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.390
I remember doing a video book report

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.970
of "The Pushcart War" in third grade.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.550
And my grandmothers in it,
my great-grandmothers in it.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.750
They all played teachers.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:22.583
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:23.550
- And my mom was in it,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.860
and I made them act out
scenes from the book,

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.380
and filmed it with like a huge camcorder.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.820
- I love forced family fun.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:30.653
Yeah.

00:01:30.653 --> 00:01:31.486
(studio audience laughing)

00:01:31.486 --> 00:01:32.319
It's awesome.

00:01:32.319 --> 00:01:34.020
We actually have this
video, so let's see a bit.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:34.853
- [Lin-Manuel] Fantastic.

00:01:34.853 --> 00:01:37.270
- The teachers need tax for the classes.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.768
For your convenient, we have hired people

00:01:39.768 --> 00:01:44.373
to play the role of teachers on strike.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:46.783
- [Teachers] No tax!

00:01:46.783 --> 00:01:48.006
(teachers chanting)

00:01:48.006 --> 00:01:49.083
- [Lin-Manuel] What is
the meaning of this?

00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:51.120
- [Teacher 1] Mr. Mayor,
we don't think it's fair

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.090
that you be taxing our tax, the tax.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:58.920
We not breaking the tires on your truck.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.380
You should find out who's
responsible for that,

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.760
and make them pay.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.090
Not us poor citizens who
have to teach in schools.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.584
And now we have to spend our money to buy,

00:02:08.584 --> 00:02:10.893
to pay extra tax on tax, no tax.

00:02:10.893 --> 00:02:14.413
(teachers chanting)

00:02:14.413 --> 00:02:15.584
- Oh my God.

00:02:15.584 --> 00:02:16.417
(studio audience cheering)

00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:17.743
- Tour de force performance.

00:02:17.743 --> 00:02:20.820
- Your mother, I see where
you get your passion.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.080
- My mom was so committed to,

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.995
you can tell I'm genuinely
scared of that video.

00:02:23.995 --> 00:02:25.200
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.250
I knew what was happening.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.420
I told her what to say to me.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.340
But then she gave it such ferocity.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.110
- She is, I see where you get it from.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.580
- Yeah, I'm like against the wall

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.840
with my little mayor's hat.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.673
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:02:34.673 --> 00:02:37.410
She was full on yelling
at you on, but wait.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.170
So today marks the start
of Hispanic Heritage Month.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.870
So what does this month
mean to you, specifically?

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.450
- Well, I, I think for
me and for all of us,

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.000
it's a great way to showcase the diversity

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.380
that is the Latino experience.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.480
It's, you know, we're not one country.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.820
We come in, all colors, and
all shapes, and all sizes.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.235
And we're 30 some odd countries.

00:02:55.235 --> 00:02:56.068
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:56.068 --> 00:02:58.530
- And it's about sharing
what makes us distinct.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.496
And also like all the
many things we share.

00:03:00.496 --> 00:03:03.090
- It's great for us too,
that aren't of that culture.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.980
But we get to experience
it because of this month.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:05.813
- [Lin-Manuel] Yeah.

00:03:05.813 --> 00:03:06.900
- We get to see stuff that
maybe we wouldn't have known

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:07.830
and learn stuff.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.210
So I, it's important for everyone.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.330
So with "Encanto", you
celebrated the Hispanic family,

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.300
and generational trauma
was kind of a major theme.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.133
- Yeah.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:16.966
Well, it's funny.

00:03:16.966 --> 00:03:17.799
I remember talking to you,

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:19.440
I think the week before it came out

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.500
- Dude, I love you so much.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.333
You're so talented.

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:24.166
I don't, I don't think,

00:03:24.166 --> 00:03:26.220
you know a person that
seen that movie more

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.880
than myself because of my kids.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:28.950
- Well, I remember,

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.960
I remember the week
before it came out also,

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:35.115
I did your show and I met
someone and his name was Bruno.

00:03:35.115 --> 00:03:35.948
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:38.046
And I said, you're not
gonna understand this,

00:03:38.046 --> 00:03:39.900
(Kelly laughing)
(studio audience laughing)

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.970
but I'm so sorry.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.140
I'm just, I'm just remember I
said, I'm sorry, in advance.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.576
- [Kelly] It's like any girl named Jolene.

00:03:47.576 --> 00:03:50.010
- Yeah, Jolene or Bruno.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.896
Eliza's, I am sorry.

00:03:51.896 --> 00:03:52.729
- Yeah.

00:03:52.729 --> 00:03:55.050
I love that, that's hysterical, but,

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.490
but speaking of "Encanto,"

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.486
is it true that Bruno
originally had a different name?

00:03:58.486 --> 00:03:59.319
- Yeah.

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:01.890
Bruno in the early drafts was named Oscar.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.270
- [Kelly] I can't hear that now.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.126
- Yeah, well.

00:04:04.126 --> 00:04:04.959
(Kelly singing)

00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:05.954
♪ You don't know about Oscar ♪

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:06.787
- Oscar, Kirk, Kirk, Kirk.

00:04:06.787 --> 00:04:07.710
Yeah, it doesn't sing.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:08.915
- [Kelly] Yeah, Bruno sounds-

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.010
- Yeah, and then they found
out that Oscar Madrigal

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.570
was like a super common name,

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.120
or like a taken name in Colombia.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.460
And so they, they gave me
like three other finalists.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.094
And as soon as I saw
Bruno, I was like, got it.

00:04:19.094 --> 00:04:19.927
- Yeah.

00:04:19.927 --> 00:04:20.880
- I got the whole song.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.713
- Yeah.

00:04:21.713 --> 00:04:23.370
- I got Bruno and I can
play with the no, no, no.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.240
And I'm done.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.073
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:25.073 --> 00:04:25.934
- Thank you for writing this song for me.

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:26.767
- [Kelly] Great vowel.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:28.050
Is a great vow to sing, really.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.360
Yeah, I like to change those up sometimes,

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.934
and they're like that's
not how you pronounce it.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.000
I don't care.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:33.833
All right.

00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:34.980
So you have a new movie coming out

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.480
and it's about two Mexican-American boys.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.500
And can you tell us about it?

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.333
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:42.427
This is this was this beautiful
young adult novel called

00:04:42.427 --> 00:04:45.450
"Aristotle and Dante Discover
the Secrets of the Universe."

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.490
And I was lucky enough
to be the actor hired

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.955
to recite the audio book years ago.

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:50.850
- Oh wow, yeah.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.544
- It's a beautiful coming of age story,

00:04:52.544 --> 00:04:56.075
about these two Mexican
teenagers, Aristotle and Dante.

00:04:56.075 --> 00:04:59.850
The filmmaker, H. Alberto
had an amazing screenplay,

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.920
and she had a vision to,
to put it up on screen.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.990
And I, I realized like, oh,

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.610
my job is to help you get this made.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:06.900
So I'm a producer on the movie.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:07.766
- Yeah.

00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:09.450
- It's a beautiful movie and
it'll come out next year,

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.430
just premiered at the
Toronto film festival

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.530
and it'll be out soon.

